This happened to me, too.  I think I've figured out why, though...

It seems that when you leave something sitting next to a large body of water
(f'rinstance, a moat), the water has a tendency to seep through the ground
and rust it, or something to that effect.  I left a bag of goodies right
in front of the moat of the castle whilst proceeding to slice-n-dice
its inhabitants, and when I came back, all the potions had turned to 
water, the scrolls and spellbooks were blank, and the weapons were
rusty.  (And I had Mjolly in there, too!  I'd found it "very rusty"
on the Medusa level and hadn't bothered to enchant it yet).  Luckily,
rustproofing your weapons and/or armor also seems to correct their
current rusted status.  

I have, by the way, seen (and fought) an angel.  They're not so tough. :)
The one mind flayer I encountered sent "waves of mental energy" over me,
then promptly died as I struck him.  No apparent effect.  What are they
*supposed* to do?  

Two questions:  1) I already know how to make (and have made) a crysknife,
but mine reverted back to a worm tooth after a while.  Is there something
else you should do besides use the scroll of enchant weapon?  I know in
3.0j it reverted to a tooth if you tried to rustproof it (at least, mine
always did).  Perhaps it's because I put it down while sorting through 
all my stuff?  2)  How do you make dragon armor again?  Thanks to Fort 
Ludios, I now have three sets of gray dragon scales, and I'd like to make
something of them.  I saw a description of how to do this in another
post, but can't seem to find the post.  

